<title>BELGIUM: EU 1996-98 ECONOMIC FORECAST FOR BELGIUM.</title>
<headline>EU 1996-98 ECONOMIC FORECAST FOR BELGIUM.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the economic</p>
<p>forecasts by the European Commission for Belgium -</p>
<p>				     1996	 1997     1998</p>
<p> GDP growth (pct)		1.4	  2.2	2.7</p>
<p> Investment			3.8	  5.8	4.9</p>
<p> GDP price deflator (pct)    2.0	  2.1	2.0</p>
<p> Unemployment (pct)	    9.9	  9.9	9.8</p>
<p> Public sector deficit*	3.3	  2.9	2.5</p>
<p> Debt/GDP ratio		130.6	127.0    123.9</p>
<p> Current account balance*    4.1	  4.5	5.2</p>
<p>(*pct of GDP)</p>
<p>Note: Projections for 1998 are essentially an extrapolation</p>
<p>of expected trends in 1997 and are based on the assumption of</p>
<p>unchanged policies, the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
